# {{PROJECT_NAME}}: Deploy

Implement contract `release-deploy/v1` for this repository only.

## Project Contract

```text
Repository: {{REPOSITORY_PATH}}
Release policy: <repo>/.agents/policies/release.yaml (consumed by $release)
Environments: test | production
Deployment system: {{DEPLOYMENT_SYSTEM}}
```

Never infer the target from the current checkout, current host, or ambient
provider selection. Resolve and report the exact {{TARGET_IDENTITY_FIELDS}}
before mutation.

## Inputs

```yaml
contract: release-deploy/v1
project: {{PROJECT_NAME}}
repo: {{REPOSITORY_PATH}}
action: deploy | verify
environment: test | production
requested_ref: <full commit SHA>
release_tag: <immutable tag or null>
release_pr: <URL or null>
authorization: <user-authorized scope>
```

Reject an abbreviated, missing, or unresolved `requested_ref`. A branch name is
context, not an immutable deployment identity.

## Capabilities

| Environment | Deployment | Verify-only | Trigger |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| test | {{TEST_DEPLOY_SUPPORT}} | {{TEST_VERIFY_SUPPORT}} | {{TEST_TRIGGER}} |
| production | {{PRODUCTION_DEPLOY_SUPPORT}} | {{PRODUCTION_VERIFY_SUPPORT}} | {{PRODUCTION_TRIGGER}} |

GitHub Release publication triggers deployment: {{GITHUB_RELEASE_TRIGGER}}

## Preconditions And Authorization

{{PRECONDITIONS_AND_AUTHORIZATION}}

Name required credentials or login state, but never print or persist secret
values. A `verify` request is read-only and must not be upgraded to `deploy`.
Rollback is a separate mutation and requires its own authorization unless an
already-approved project policy explicitly owns it.

