## Revision Integrity, Health, And Smoke Checks

{{INTEGRITY_HEALTH_SMOKE}}

Success requires runtime proof that the observed revision matches
`requested_ref` or a documented deterministic immutable equivalent. A completed
upload, build, restart, or provider job alone is not deployment success.

## Retry, Stop, And Rollback

{{RETRY_STOP_ROLLBACK}}

Do not blindly retry non-idempotent deployments, migrations, submissions, or
rollbacks. Return `blocked` or `failed` with evidence when the safe boundary is
reached.

## Receipt

```yaml
contract: release-deploy/v1
project: {{PROJECT_NAME}}
action: deploy | verify
environment: test | production
status: deployed | verified | blocked | failed | rolled-back
requested_ref: <full commit SHA>
observed_ref: <full running commit SHA or immutable equivalent>
release_tag: <tag or null>
deployment_id: <provider/run/deployment id or null>
started_at: <timestamp or null>
finished_at: <timestamp or null>
checks:
  build: passed | failed | not-applicable
  migration: passed | failed | not-applicable
  rollout: passed | failed | not-applicable
  health: passed | failed | not-applicable
  smoke: passed | failed | not-applicable
rollback:
  supported: {{ROLLBACK_SUPPORTED}}
  target: <immutable ref or null>
  performed: true | false
evidence:
  - <redacted provider/runtime proof>
notes:
  - <remaining risk or none>
```
